City Re-Draft 04/06/11
City REDRAFT
04/06/11

UP Folder Number 2481-05

EASEMENT AGREEMENT

THIS Easement Deed and Agreement ("Agreement") is made and entered into as of the ____
day of ___________________, 2011 , by and between UNION PACIFIC RAILROAD COMPANY,
a Delaware corporation ("Grantor"), and CITY OF CHEYENNE, a municipal corporation of the
State of Wyoming ("Grantee").

RECITALS

Grantee, under its Project RFP-3-07, Contract 5033 (the "Project") has
requested Grantor's permission to construct, use, maintain, repair and renew a portion
of Grantee's East Cheyenne Greenway Phase III Project trail (the "Trail") on, along
and across Grantor's property in the location shown on the survey and Grantor's print,
each marked Exhibit A and as described in the legal description marked Exhibit A-
1, with each exhibit being attached hereto and hereby made a part hereof (the
"Easement Area").

The plans for the Trail are marked Exhibit B, attached hereto and hereby
made a part hereof (the "Plans").

This Agreement is made to cover the construction, use, maintenance, repair
and renewal of the Trail on, along and across the Easement Area.

AGREEMENT

Grantor and Grantee hereby mutually agree as follows:

Section 1.
GRANT OF EASEMENT

A.
Grantor, for and in consideration of the sum of Six Thousand Five Hundred Dollars
($6,500.00), to it paid by Grantee, the receipt whereof is hereby acknowledged, grants to Grantee, its
successors and assigns, an EASEMENT ("Easement") upon, along and across the Easement Area for
the operation and maintenance of a ten (10) foot wide concrete recreational, pedestrian and bicycle
trail and associated drainage facilities and fencing, only, for the purpose of the rights herein granted.
The Easement is subject to the limitations set forth in this Agreement.

B.
The Easement herein granted is for recreational, pedestrian and bicycle trail purposes
only.  Without limitation of the foregoing, this grant does not include the right to install utilities of
```

### Page 2 of 12

```text
City Re-Draft 04/06/11
any nature, including, without limitation, fiber optic, cable television, electrical, gas or liquid
distribution, and telephone lines, except for electrical lines needed for Trail lighting.

C.
RESERVING, however, unto the Grantor, its successors and assigns, the right to
construct at any and all times and to maintain railroad tracks, track appurtenances, fiber optic or
signal lines and facilities, pipe, telephone, and electric pole and wire lines, over, under and across the
Easement Area, but in such a way as to not unreasonably interfere with Grantee's use of the
Easement Area, for the purposes specified in this Agreement; it being understood that the rights so
reserved unto the Grantor, its successors and assigns, are retained along with the general right of the
Grantor, its successors and assigns, to the use of the Easement Area, for any purpose not inconsistent
with Grantee's use of the Easement Area, for the purposes herein defined, including, but not limited
to any and all general railroad purposes.

D.
The Easement is also limited to such rights as the Grantor may have in the Easement
Area and is granted without warranty, express or implied.  No damages shall be recoverable from
Grantor because of any dispossession of the Grantee or because of failure of, or defect in, Grantor's
title.

E.
This Easement is also made SUBJECT TO all outstanding leases, licenses and other
outstanding rights, including, but not limited to, those for pipelines, wirelines and roadways and the
right of renewals and extensions of the same (whether recorded or unrecorded) and also subject to all
conditions, limitations, restrictions, encumbrances, reservations or interests of any person which may
affect the Easement Area, whether recorded or unrecorded.

Section 2.
NO PROJECT COSTS TO BE BORNE BY GRANTOR

Grantee confirms that Grantor shall not bear any Project costs nor shall Grantor be required
to provide any funding for the Project.

Section 3.
CONSTRUCTION OF TRAIL

A.
Grantee, at its expense, will completely fund the administration, design and
construction of the Trail including, without limitation, construction contract administration of the
Project, construction phasing and traffic control and Federal, State and Local permitting.

B.
Grantor has approved the Plans for the Trail, provided Grantor's review shall be for its
own purposes and benefit, and Grantor shall not be deemed liable to any other party for defects in
any Plans or plan approval by Grantor.

C.
Grantee, at its expense, shall (i) construct the Trail within the Easement Area in full
compliance with the Plans, (ii) provide, maintain and keep clear of obstruction adequate drainage to
preserve the natural and pre-existing drainage patterns for both the Trail and also the College Drive
overpass structure above the Trail to ensure that the drainage from the overpass and Trail will not
interfere with or damage Grantor=s property adjacent to or near the Easement Area, including
Grantor's tracks and right of way, (iii) provide, maintain, repair and renew adequate lighting of the
Trail within the Easement Area, (iv) erect, maintain, repair and renew a 10-foot by 12-foot enclosed
black vinyl coated chain link fencing on all portions of the Trail that are located within the Easement
```

### Page 3 of 12

```text
City Re-Draft 04/06/11
Area, and (v) provide, maintain, repair and renew lighting (as approved by Grantor) under the
College Drive overpass at locations on Railroad=s property other than on the Easement Area.

D.
As part of this Project, Grantee, at its expense and simultaneously within the same
Project scheduled completion period, shall also replace the Railroad=s existing north right of way 4-
strand barb wire fencing located within the Project limits and west of College Drive with a chain link
fence that matches the seven (7) foot height of the existing chain link fencing separating Railroad=s
right of way from the Henderson Basin detention facility located on the east side of College Drive;
with such fencing to be constructed in the locations shown and described on Exhibit B.  Grantee
must obtain Railroad=s written approval of the fencing plans prior to Grantee constructing such
fencing.  As part of this Project, Grantee, at its expense, shall also reasonably compact and seed
within the Easement Area any disturbed areas due to the construction of the Trail.

E.
As part of this Project, Grantee, at its expense, shall also replace Grantor=s existing
seven (7) foot high chain link fencing along Grantee=s future Greenway trail path which is to be
constructed within the adjacent 250-foot wide (plus or minus) corridor north of Grantor=s main line
tracks between the western limits of the Grantee=s current Greenway Phase III project and the
location of Grantee=s Norris Avenue overpass structure to the west.  The fencing described in the
preceding sentence shall be located in the locations shown on Exhibit B and construction of such
fencing shall occur when Grantee is constructing such future Greenway trail improvements.  Grantee
shall not commence the construction of such fencing until Grantor has provided Grantee the
Grantor=s written approval of such fencing plans.

F.
Grantee, at its expense, shall provide Grantor with a complete set of "as-built"
construction drawings of the Trail within the Easement Area upon Grantee=s completion of such
construction.

Section 4.
USE, MAINTENANCE AND REPAIR OF TRAIL AND FENCING

Grantee, at its expense, shall maintain, repair and renew the entire Trail within the Easement
Area and also all fencing described in Section 3 above.  Such maintenance shall include, without
limitation, all upkeep involving the Trail and fencing, law enforcement to prevent trespassing onto
Railroad=s adjacent property, sanitation, trash removal, drainage and regulation of hours of use and
graffiti removal.

Section 5.
WORK TO BE PERFORMED BY GRANTOR; BILLING
SENT TO GRANTEE; GRANTEE=S PAYMENT OF BILLING

A.
Grantor, at Grantee=s expense, shall perform the work described in Grantor=s estimate
dated January 14, 2010, marked Exhibit C, attached hereto and hereby made a part hereof.

B.
Grantor shall send billing to Grantee within one hundred eighty (180) days after
receiving written notice from Grantee that all Project work within any portion of Railroad=s right of
way has been completed.
```

