```text
City Re-Draft 04/06/11
C.
Grantee shall pay Grantor for all actual costs incurred by Grantor, including Grantor's
customary additives, in connection with this Project within thirty (30) days of receipt of billing from
Grantor.

Section 6.
CONTRACTOR=S RIGHT OF ENTRY AGREEMENT

A.
Grantee shall require its contractor(s) that will be performing any Project work on
Grantor=s right of way (including initial construction and any subsequent maintenance and repair
work) to execute the Grantor=s then current Contractor=s Right of Entry Agreement and to obtain and
provide to Grantor the insurance policies, binders, certificates and endorsements that are required in
such Contractor=s Right of Entry Agreement prior to allowing its contractor(s) to commence any
work on Grantor=s right of way.

B.
Grantee confirms that it has received from Grantor the Grantor=s current form of
Contractor=s Right of Entry Agreement.

Section 7.
INDEMNITY

A.
Grantee, to the extent it may lawfully do so, for itself, its successors and assigns,
agrees to indemnify, defend and hold harmless Grantor and its affiliates, and their officers, agents,
employees, successors and assigns, against and from any and all liability, loss, damage, claims,
demands, actions, causes of action, costs and expenses of whatsoever nature, including court costs
and attorney's fees, which may result from personal injury to or death of persons whomsoever, or
damage to or loss or destruction of property whatsoever, when such personal injury, death, loss,
destruction or damage grows out of or arises from (i) the presence of the Trail within the Easement
Area, (ii) the exercise by the general public or by Grantee, its agents, employees, contractors,
licensees or invitees of any of the rights herein granted with respect to the Easement, or (iii) the
breach by Grantee of this Agreement, in each case regardless of any negligence of Grantor, its
officers, agents or employees, provided however, that the Grantee shall not be subjected to liability
for judgments, damages, costs, attorney=s fees or other damages or  expense to the extent the
Grantee=s liability would exceed Ten Million Dollars ($10,000,000.00) per accident or occurrence.

B.
To the extent it may lawfully do so, as between Grantor and Grantee, and subject to
the limitations specified in Section 7A of this Easement Agreement, Grantee hereby waives its
governmental immunity by entering into this  Easement  Agreement, provided however, that Grantee
retains all immunities and defenses available to Grantee as a governmental entity pursuant to the
Wyoming Governmental Claims Act, W.S. §§ 1-39-101, et seq., to the extent that the Grantee’s
liability would exceed Ten Million Dollars ($10,000,000.00) for any accident or occurrence,
regardless of the number of claims arising from the occurrence.  Grantee acknowledges its
obligations set forth in Section 8 below are intended to effect the extension of liability of Grantee
hereunder to the maximum extent permitted under W.S. § 1-39-118(b) of the Wyoming
Governmental Claims Act.  Nothing in this Easement Agreement shall be construed as a waiver of
Grantee=s governmental immunity to the extent that the Grantee=s liability would exceed Ten Million
Dollars ($10,000,000.00) per accident or occurrence.
```

### Page 5 of 12

```text
City Re-Draft 04/06/11
Section 8.
INSURANCE

Grantee shall, at its own sole cost and expense, procure the following kinds of insurance and
promptly pay when due all premiums for that insurance.  The following insurance, unless otherwise
specified in this Agreement, shall be kept in force by Grantee and Grantee's successors until such
time as Grantee records a written release of this Agreement in the public real estate records of
Laramie County, Wyoming, and removes the Trail from the Easement Area in a manner approved by
Grantor.  Grantee shall provide to Grantor a certificate of insurance issued by a duly authorized
insurer as follows:

Commercial general liability (CGL) insurance with a limit of not less than $10,000,000 for
each accident or occurrence, regardless of the number of claims which may arise from an occurrence.
CGL insurance must be written on ISO occurrence form CG 00 01 12 04 or a substitute form
providing equivalent coverage.

Business auto liability coverage written on ISO form CA 00 01 10 01, or a substitute form
providing equivalent coverage, with a limit of not less $2,000,000 for each accident, and coverage
must include liability arising out of any auto (including owned, hired, and non-owned autos) at any
time there is a city or city contractor’s auto (auto as defined by the required ISO Business Auto
insurance form, or a substitute form providing equivalent coverage) is on or within fifty (50) feet of
railroad property for the purpose of construction or maintenance in connection with this Agreement.

Workers Compensation and Employers Liability insurance in accordance with the Wyoming
statutes and the Wyoming Workers Compensation Fund.

Grantee shall include Grantor as an additional insured with respect to all insurable liabilities
arising out of Grantee's obligations to Grantor in this Agreement using ISO Additional Insured
Endorsement CG 20 26 (or a substitute form providing equivalent coverage).  Additional Insured
coverage shall be primary and noncontributory with respect to any insurance carried by Grantor.

The fact that insurance is obtained by Grantee on behalf of Grantor will not be deemed to
release or diminish the liability of Grantee, including, without limitation, liability under the
indemnity provisions of this Agreement.  Damages recoverable by Grantor from Grantee or any third
party will not be limited by the amount of the required insurance coverage, unless limited by statue,
including the Wyoming Governmental Claims Act.

Section 9.
TERMINATION ON DEFAULT

Grantor may terminate this Agreement if Grantee fails to cure any material default of the
terms of this Agreement, and after written notice is given by Grantor to Grantee specifying the
default, Grantee fails either to immediately commence to cure the default, or to complete the cure
expeditiously but in all events within thirty (30) days after the default notice is given.
```

### Page 6 of 12

```text
City Re-Draft 04/06/11
Section 10.
ABANDONMENT

If Grantee, its successors or assigns, shall abandon the Easement Area for the purposes of this
Easement, then this Agreement and the rights herein granted shall cease automatically and terminate,
and the title to the Easement Area shall be freed from the burden of this Easement.  It is further
agreed that nonuse of the Easement Area for the purposes of this Easement for a continuous period
of one (1) year shall be deemed an abandonment of the Easement Area.

Section 11.
NOTICES

Any notices required or desired to be given under this Agreement shall be in writing and
personally served, given by overnight express delivery, or given by mail.  Telecopy notices shall be
deemed valid only to the extent they are (a) actually received by the individual to whom addressed
and (b) followed by delivery of actual notice in the manner described above within three (3) business
days thereafter.  Any notice given by mail shall be sent, postage prepaid, by certified mail, return
receipt requested, addressed to the party to receive at the following address or at such other address
as the party may from time to time direct in writing:

Grantor:

UNION PACIFIC RAILROAD COMPANY
Real Estate Department
Attn: Assistant Vice President-Real Estate
1400 Douglas Street, MS 1690
Omaha, Nebraska  68179
Facsimile:  (402) 501-0340

Grantee:

CITY OF CHEYENNE
Attn: Richard L. Kaysen
Mayor,
2101 O’Neil Avenue
Cheyenne, WY 82001
Facsimile: 307-637-6378

Express delivery notices shall be deemed to be given upon receipt.  Postal notices shall be deemed to
be given three (3) days after deposit with the United States Postal Service.

Section 12.
RESTORATION OF RAILROAD=S PROPERTY UPON TERMINATION.

In the event of termination howsoever of this Easement, (i) Grantee shall deliver to Grantor a
recordable instrument evidencing that the title to the Easement Area is free and clear of the burden of
this Easement and is free and clear of liens, encumbrances, clouds upon or defects in the title created
or permitted to be created by Grantee, and (ii) within thirty (30) days after receipt of notice from
Grantor to perform such activities, Grantee shall remove the Trail and all appurtenances constructed
on the Easement Area and restore the Easement Area to its original condition, failing in which
Grantor may perform such activities at Grantee's expense.
```

